      "provider": "ollama",
      "model": "mycoder-v0.2",
      "prompt": "You are helping with the following request:\n\ngive me a detailed prompt to build a simple farming loop\n\nRespond using exactly these markdown section headers, in this order, each followed by concise content (use bullet points where helpful):\n\n## Goal\n## Milestones\n## Tasks\n## Risks & Mitigations\n\nDo not add any extra top-level headers or preamble text before the first header.",
      "response": "## Goal\n- Build a self-sustaining farming loop that can produce food without relying on external inputs for an extended period.\n- The system should be able to cultivate crops, raise livestock, and recycle waste into compost to support future growth.\n- Ensure the loop is efficient, sustainable, and minimizes environmental impact.\n\n## Milestones\n1. **Research and Planning**\n   - Identify the types of crops and livestock suitable for the local climate and soil.\n   - Design the layout of the farming area to optimize space and resource use.\n2. **Infrastructure Setup**\n   - Construct necessary structures such as greenhouses, barns, and storage facilities.\n   - Install irrigation systems, composting facilities, and other essential equipment.\n3. **Initial Planting and Livestock Introduction**\n   - Start with a small variety of crops to diversify the farm's output.\n   - Introduce a small number of livestock to begin the cycle.\n4. **Monitoring and Adjustment**\n   - Regularly monitor crop health, livestock well-being, and overall system performance.\n   - Make adjustments to the farming practices based on observations and feedback.\n5. **Full Cycle Operation**\n   - Achieve a point where all outputs from the farm (e.g., manure, crop residues) are recycled back into the system.\n   - Ensure the farm is capable of producing enough food to sustain itself over time.\n\n## Tasks\n1. **Market Research**\n   - Conduct surveys and studies to understand local agricultural needs and market demands.\n   - Identify potential crops and livestock breeds that can thrive in the region.\n2. **Design and Layout**\n   - Create detailed blueprints for the farming area, including water management, waste recycling, and energy use.\n   - Allocate spaces for different activities like planting, animal husbandry, and processing.\n3. **Resource Procurement**\n   - Purchase seeds, livestock, tools, and materials needed for the initial setup.\n   - Secure funding or grants for large-scale infrastructure projects.\n4. **Construction and Installation**\n   - Build structures according to the design specifications.\n   - Set up irrigation, composting, and other systems.\n5. **Planting and Livestock Introduction**\n   - Begin sowing seeds and nurturing young plants.\n   - Acclimate livestock to their new environment and provide necessary care.\n6. **Monitoring and Maintenance**\n   - Establish a routine for checking crop health, watering needs, and animal welfare.\n   - Collect data on crop yields, livestock productivity, and resource usage.\n7. **Feedback Loop**\n   - Analyze collected data to identify areas for improvement.\n   - Adjust farming techniques, crop rotations, and livestock management strategies.\n8. **Sustainability Assessment**\n   - Regularly evaluate the farm’s sustainability practices.\n   - Implement measures to reduce waste, conserve resources, and enhance biodiversity.\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n- **Climate Variability**: \n  - Mitigation: Choose crops and livestock that are resilient to local weather conditions. Implement irrigation systems that can adapt to changing rainfall patterns.\n- **Disease Outbreak**:\n  - Mitigation: Maintain strict hygiene protocols in livestock areas. Use organic pest control methods for crops. Rotate crops to prevent disease buildup.\n- **Market Fluctuations**:\n  - Mitigation: Diversify the range of crops and livestock to spread risk. Develop a marketing plan to ensure products are sold at a steady rate.\n- **Technological Failure**:\n  - Mitigation: Regularly maintain and update all farm equipment. Have backup plans in case of system failures.\n- **Resource Scarcity**:\n  - Mitigation: Implement water-saving techniques such as drip irrigation. Recycle water and nutrients through composting and anaerobic digestion.",
      "tokens_used": 1032,
      "duration_ms": 83809,
      "created_at": 1784010509
    },
    {
      "id": "ea868626-3edb-46a3-804f-7a92ec07f20a",
