      "model": "mycoder-v0.2",
      "prompt": "You are helping with the following request:\n\ngive me a detailed prompt to build a simple farming loop\n\nRespond using exactly these markdown section headers, in this order, each followed by concise content (use bullet points where helpful):\n\n## Goal\n## Milestones\n## Tasks\n## Risks & Mitigations\n\nDo not add any extra top-level headers or preamble text before the first header.",
      "response": "## Goal\n- Build a basic farming simulation loop that allows a player to plant, grow, and harvest crops.\n- The loop should include a planting phase, a growing phase, and a harvesting phase.\n- The player should be able to choose which crop to plant and see the progress of their crops over time.\n- The simulation should include basic weather conditions that affect crop growth.\n\n## Milestones\n1. **Design the Farming System**\n   - Define the data structures for crops, weather, and farm plots.\n   - Outline the user interface elements needed for planting, growing, and harvesting.\n\n2. **Implement Planting Phase**\n   - Allow the player to select a crop from a list of available options.\n   - Place the selected crop on an available farm plot.\n\n3. **Implement Growing Phase**\n   - Simulate the growth of crops over time, taking into account weather conditions.\n   - Update the UI to reflect the growth progress of each crop.\n\n4. **Implement Harvesting Phase**\n   - Allow the player to harvest fully grown crops.\n   - Remove the harvested crop from the farm plot and update the inventory.\n\n5. **Integrate Weather Effects**\n   - Randomly generate weather conditions (e.g., sunny, rainy, stormy) that affect crop growth.\n   - Adjust the growth rate based on the current weather condition.\n\n6. **Testing and Debugging**\n   - Test the entire farming loop to ensure all phases work correctly.\n   - Debug any issues found during testing.\n\n## Tasks\n1. **Define Data Structures**\n   - Create a `Crop` class with properties like name, growth stage, and yield.\n   - Create a `Weather` class with properties like condition and effect on growth.\n   - Create a `FarmPlot` class with properties like location and current crop.\n\n2. **Design User Interface**\n   - Sketch out the layout for the planting, growing, and harvesting screens.\n   - Decide on the controls for selecting crops and interacting with farm plots.\n\n3. **Implement Planting Logic**\n   - Write the function to handle crop selection.\n   - Write the function to place a crop on a farm plot.\n\n4. **Implement Growing Logic**\n   - Write the function to simulate crop growth over time.\n   - Update the UI to show the growth progress of each crop.\n\n5. **Implement Harvesting Logic**\n   - Write the function to check if a crop is ready for harvest.\n   - Write the function to remove the harvested crop from the farm plot and update the inventory.\n\n6. **Implement Weather Simulation**\n   - Write the function to randomly generate weather conditions.\n   - Write the function to adjust crop growth based on the current weather condition.\n\n7. **Testing and Debugging**\n   - Run the farming loop through multiple iterations.\n   - Check for any bugs or unexpected behavior.\n   - Fix any issues found and retest.\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n- **Risk:** Overcomplication of the farming system leading to high development time.\n  - **Mitigation:** Start with a minimal set of features and gradually add complexity.\n- **Risk:** Inaccurate simulation of crop growth due to random weather effects.\n  - **Mitigation:** Test the weather simulation thoroughly and adjust the growth rates accordingly.\n- **Risk:** Bugs in the UI causing issues with user interaction.\n  - **Mitigation:** Conduct frequent UI tests and gather feedback from users.\n- **Risk:** Performance issues when simulating large farms with many crops.\n  - **Mitigation:** Optimize the code to handle multiple crops efficiently and consider parallel processing if necessary.",
      "tokens_used": 960,
      "duration_ms": 826696,
      "created_at": 1784010457
    },
