      "model": "mycoder-v0.2",
      "prompt": "\nOpen Questions\n\n    Should the declaredValueUSD parameter be enforced? Leaving it optional means the caller controls whether to declare value, which is accurate since not all carriers require it. Declaring value is a soft hint, not a requirement.\n\nOllama (local)·Project Map427 tokens · 06:09 PM\nOverview\n\nBuild a lightweight Node.js module named shippo-rates that exposes a single method: chooseRate. This method takes an object { rateId, weightKg, declaredValueUSD }, calls the Shippo API to confirm the selected rate is still valid for those parameters, and returns it directly on success. On failure, throw a descriptive error (rate expired, carrier no longer offers it, etc.) so the caller can re-prompt.\nKey Components\n\n    lib/api.js: wraps the official Shippo SDK, exposing only what's needed.\n    lib/confirm-rate.js: does the live-check against the current rates.\n    index.js: the one-line chooseRate entry point.\n    test/index.js: mocks the API and tests the logic comprehensively.\n\nDependencies\n\nnpm install @shippo/sdk\n\nOpen Questions\n\n    The declaredValueUSD parameter is optional; should we enforce its presence?\n    If absent, the live check will fail if the rate requires it.\n    Leaving it optional means the caller has full control over whether to declare value.\n    Declaring value is _not_ required by all carriers/rates, so it's a soft hint.\n    We could document this behavior but don't _enforce_ it programmatically.\n",
      "response": "```js\nexport async function chooseRate({ rateId, weightKg, declaredValueUSD }) {\n  const sdk = await getShippo();\n  try {\n    // Confirm the selected rate is still valid for these params.\n    const confirmed = await sdk.call('rate.confirm', {\n      rate: rateId,\n      weight_kg: weightKg,\n      declared_value_usd: declaredValueUSD ?? null,\n    });\n    return confirmed;\n  } catch (err) {\n    if (err.code === 'RATE_EXPIRED') throw new Error(`Rate ${rateId} expired.`);\n    if (err.code === 'CARRIER_NO_LONGER_OFFERS_RATE')\n      throw new Error(`Carrier no longer offers ${rateId}.`);\n    throw err;\n  }\n}\n```",
