      "prompt": "You are helping with the following request:\n\nOverviewThe drawWorldLayer module draws the entire project map for an 8-bit-style platformer. Every line of code you see here is what runs; no imports, no external lookups — it compiles as given. Comments call out every architectural decision and rationale so you can follow along and understand why things are the way they are.\nComponents\n\n    drawSky: gradient sky with a distant haze band.\n    drawClouds: three tiers of white rects at fixed offsets from the camera.\n    drawDustFloor: a sandy ground layer with occasional sand grains and a few rocks.\n    drawPitWall: a thin, dark wall with cracks and a faint glow.\n    drawRubble: random stone shapes with cracks and a gritty texture.\n    drawPressurePlate: a small hole that lights up when pressed.\n    drawDoor: two-way exit to hub or next stage.\n    drawSavePoint: a glowing heart marker.\n    drawFogBand: a vertical fog/shadow band that moves with the camera.\n    drawLightningFlash: a burst of white + flash for pickups / secrets.\n    drawPickupIcon: a label above pickups (★ / ! / #).\n    drawSecretMarker: a tiny \"S\" for hidden rooms.\n    drawOneWayPlatform: a one-way floor tile that only pushes players up.\n    drawTeleporter: a shimmering portal to the hub market.\n    drawHubPortal: a one-way door into the hub.\n\nData Flow\n\n    The level definition (levels.js) describes all features by type & ID.\n    drawWorldLayer reads this data and calls the relevant renderer per feature.\n    Drawers use the canvas context directly (ctx) to stamp geometry/textures.\n    The world moves left-to-right; each element draws relative to cam.x.\n\nTradeoffs\n\n    All rendering fits inside a single ~60-line module.\n    No external dependencies keeps it portable and easy to reason about.\n    The procedural style is entirely self-contained.\n\n\n\n\nRespond using exactly these markdown section headers, in this order, each followed by concise content (use bullet points where helpful):\n\n## Goal\n## Milestones\n## Tasks\n## Risks & Mitigations\n\nDo not add any extra top-level headers or preamble text before the first header.",
      "response": "## Goal\nDraw the entire project map for an 8-bit-style platformer, handling every visible feature from the level definition without importing anything.\n\n## Milestones\n1. Implement `drawSky` with a gradient sky and distant haze.\n2. Code `drawClouds` for three-tiered cloud layers.\n3. Write `drawDustFloor`, including sand grains and rocks.\n4. Build `drawPitWall` with cracks and a subtle glow.\n5. Create `drawRubble` for broken stone shapes.\n6. Add `drawPressurePlate`, showing a lit hole.\n7. Draw `drawDoor` for hub/world exits.\n8. Implement `drawSavePoint` as a glowing heart.\n9. Code `drawFogBand` for the moving vertical shadow strip.\n10. Write `drawLightningFlash` for visual pickups/secrets.\n11. Create `drawPickupIcon` to show pickup labels.\n12. Build `drawSecretMarker` for hidden-room markers.\n13. Add `drawOneWayPlatform`, marking one-way floors.\n14. Implement `drawTeleporter` for hub portals.\n15. Code `drawHubPortal` for one-way world->hub doors.\n\n## Tasks\n- Complete `drawSky`: gradient sky + distant haze band.\n- Finish `drawClouds`: three tiers of moving white rects.\n- Write `drawDustFloor`: sandy ground + sparse rocks and grains.\n- Build `drawPitWall`: thin dark wall with crack lines and a faint edge glow.\n- Create `drawRubble`: random stone shapes with cracks.\n- Add `drawPressurePlate`: small hole that lights when pressed.\n- Draw `drawDoor`: two-way exit to hub or next stage.\n- Implement `drawSavePoint`: a glowing heart marker.\n- Code `drawFogBand`: a vertical shadow band that moves with the camera.\n- Write `drawLightningFlash`: a burst of white + flash for pickups/secrets.\n- Create `drawPickupIcon`: a label above pickups (★ / ! / #).\n- Build `drawSecretMarker`: a tiny \"S\" for hidden rooms.\n- Add `drawOneWayPlatform`: a one-way floor tile that only pushes players up.\n- Implement `drawTeleporter`: a shimmering portal to the hub market.\n- Code `drawHubPortal`: a one-way door into the hub.\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n- **All-in-one module**: Keeping everything together makes portability easy and reasoning straightforward.\n- **No imports**: Self-contained so it runs anywhere that supports canvas 2D.\n- **Procedural style**: Entirely generated from data, no asset dependencies.",
