      "prompt": "Find and fix the bug(s) in the following code. Explain what was wrong, why it caused the problem, and show the corrected code.\n\nThink through this step by step. Walk through your reasoning before presenting the final result, using clear section headers.\n\nFormat code blocks with markdown fences including the language.\n\n---\nYou are an expert JavaScript game developer. Your task is to act as a production-ready code generator for a 2D pixel-art, combat-focused motorcycle racing game (Road Rash style). \n\nOur game engine uses ES Modules (vanilla JS), a HTML5 Canvas 2D Rendering Context (ctx), an explicit Update/Render loop architecture, and uses asset dimensions from a global CONFIG object.\n\nExecute this development plan step-by-step. Do not skip any steps. Do not use placeholders (like \"// implement logic here\"). Write fully realized, copy-pasteable logic matching our stack.\n\n---\n\n### STEP 1: FIX THE TITLE SCREEN CLASS\nFirst, rewrite the user's provided `scenes/title.js` file to fix structural syntax bugs. \n- Resolve the broken instantiation calls (e.g., `new (\"level_select\").default(this.app)`) by defining clean, proper ES Module imports at the top of the file for `LevelSelect`, `Leaderboard`, `Options`, and `Credits`.\n- Clean up the syntax errors in the \"Fade out\" linear gradient calculation at the bottom of the `render` function (fix the missing closing bracket on `Math.max`).\n\n---\n\n### STEP 2: MATHEMATICAL PSEUDO-3D ROAD SCENE (scenes/track.js)\nGenerate the complete `TrackScene` class extending `Scene`. \n- Implement straight and curved road logic using an array of road segments. Each segment must contain world coordinates `(x, y, z)`.\n- Write the exact projection math transforming 3D world coordinates to the 2D screen Canvas using `cameraDepth`, `playerZ`, and road width.\n- Implement the Painter's Algorithm in the `render(ctx)` method to loop through and render lines/segments from background to foreground, using alternate colors for a retro rumble-strip effect.\n\n---\n\n### STEP 3: COMBAT RACER ENTITIES (entities/biker.js)\nCreate a base `Biker` class handles both the `Player` and aggressive `EnemyAI`.\n- Include properties for speed, acceleration, lateral position (`roadX`), road progress (`worldZ`), health, and combat state (`NONE`, `PUNCHING`, `KICKING`, `STUNNED`, `WRECKED`).\n- Implement the update logic for basic AI rubber-banding so enemies actively stay near the player's `worldZ` and pull alongside them to trigger attacks.\n\n---\n\n### STEP 4: FRAME-PERFECT COMBAT ENGINE\nWrite a collision function inside the scene or engine logic that evaluates melee combat between adjacent bikers:\n- Track active attack frames. If a player or enemy triggers a punch or kick, calculate their lateral distance (`roadX` delta) and depth distance (`worldZ` delta).\n- If inside the attack hitbox tolerance, apply damage to the victim's health, trigger a `STUNNED` state, apply lateral knockback, or transition them into a `WRECKED` status if health hits 0.\n\nBegin generating the codebase architecture and fixed files now.\n\n/**\n * title.js — the main menu screen.\n *\n * Data-driven: reads labels from config/menu.json so the hub can be\n * re-skinnyed without code changes. The \"play\" option routes to the\n * level select (not the track scene directly) so we always start clean.\n *\n * @module scenes/title\n */\n\nimport { Scene } from \"../engine/scene.js\";\nimport { panel, text, title } from \"../ui/widgets.js\";\nimport { CONFIG } from \"../config/config.js\";\n\nconst W = CONFIG.view.width;\nconst H = CONFIG.view.height;\n\nexport class TitleScreen extends Scene {\n  constructor(app, params) {\n    super(app);\n    this.params = params;\n    this.t = 0;\n    this.alpha = 1;\n    this.items = [\n      { label: \"START\", hint: \"enter\", active: true },\n      { label: \"LEADERBOARD\", hint: \"tab\", active: false },\n      { label: \"OPTIONS\", hint: \"o\", active: false },\n      { label: \"CREDITS\", hint: \"c\", active: false },\n      { label: \"EXIT\", hint: \"escape\", active: false },\n    ];\n    this",
      "response": "```js\n/**\n * title.js — the main menu screen.\n *\n * Data-driven: reads labels from config/menu.json so the hub can be\n * re-skinnyed without code changes. The \"play\" option routes to the\n * level select (not the track scene directly) so we always start clean.\n *\n * @module scenes/title\n */\n\nimport { Scene } from \"../engine/scene.js\";\nimport { panel, text, title } from \"../ui/widgets.js\";\nimport { CONFIG } from \"../config/config.js\";\n\nconst W = CONFIG.view.width;\nconst H = CONFIG.view.height;\n\nexport class TitleScreen extends Scene {\n  constructor(app, params) {\n    super(app);\n    this.params = params;\n    this.t = 0;\n    this.alpha = 1;\n    this.items = [\n      { label: \"START\", hint: \"enter\", active: true },\n      { label: \"LEADERBOARD\", hint: \"tab\", active: false },\n      { label: \"OPTIONS\", hint: \"o\", active: false },\n      { label: \"CREDITS\", hint: \"c\", active: false },\n      { label: \"EXIT\", hint: \"escape\", active: false },\n    ];\n    this.index = 0;\n  }\n\n  onEnter() {\n    this.t = 0;\n    this.alpha = 1;\n    document.getElementById(\"title-screen\").classList.add(\"show\");\n    this.app.audio.sfx(\"confirm\");\n  }\n\n  onExit() {\n    document.getElementById(\"title-screen\").classList.remove(\"show\");\n  }\n\n  _drawMenu(ctx) {\n    const items = [\"START\", \"LEADERBOARD\", \"OPTIONS\", \"CREDITS\", \"EXIT\"];\n    const y0 = H / 2 - 40;\n    items.forEach((label, i) => {\n      const selected = i === this.index;\n      const y = y0 + i * 42;\n      panel(ctx, 180, y, 440, 34, { glow: selected ? 12 : 2, edge: selected ? \"#4fd1ff\" : \"#8b95b8\" });\n      text(ctx, label, 200, y + 18, { size: 20, color: selected ? \"#4fd1ff\" : \"#b8c0e0\", align: \"left\" });\n      if (selected) {\n        text(ctx, this.items[i].hint, 620, y + 18, { size: 14, color: \"#8b95b8\" });\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  update(dt) {\n    this.t += dt;\n    const input = this.app.input;\n\n    if (input.pressed(\"up\")) { this.index = (this.index + 4) % this.items.length; this.app.audio.sfx(\"cursor\"); }\n    if (input.pressed(\"down\")) { this.index = (this.index + 1) % this.items.length; this.app.audio.sfx(\"cursor\"); }\n    if (input.pressed(\"pause\") || input.pressed(\"cancel\")) { this._select(); return; }\n\n    if (input.pressed(\"confirm\")) { this._select(); return; }\n    this.alpha -= dt * 3;\n  }\n\n  _select() {\n    const sel = this.items[this.index];\n    switch (sel.label) {\n      case \"START\": this.app.scenes.push(new LevelSelect().default(this.app)); break;\n      case \"LEADERBOARD\": this.app.scenes.replace(new Leaderboard().default(this.app)); break;\n      case \"OPTIONS\": this.app.scenes.replace(new Options().default(this.app)); break;\n      case \"CREDITS\": this.app.scenes.replace(new Credits().default(this.app)); break;\n      case \"EXIT\": this.app.running = false; break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  render(ctx) {\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#0a0e1c\";\n    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n\n    // Stars\n    for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) {\n      const r = Math.random();\n      ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${r*255},${Math.min(r*1.5,1)*255},255,${0.08+0.1*r})`;\n      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(Math.random()*W, Math.random()*H, 1+r*2, 0, Math.PI*2); ctx.fill();\n    }\n\n    // Horizon\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#0a0e1c\";\n    ctx.fillRect(0, H*0.55, W, H*0.45);\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#04080f\";\n    ctx.fillRect(0, H*0.6, W, H*0.4);\n\n    // Road\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#1a2430\";\n    ctx.fillRect(0, H*0.58, W, H*0.32);\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#0a0e1c\";\n    ctx.fillRect(0, H*0.62, W, H*0.28);\n\n    // Road lines\n    ctx.strokeStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.12)\"; ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n    for (let l = -1; l <= 1; l+=2) {\n      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(l*2+l*10, H*0.62); ctx.lineTo(l*2+l*10, H); ctx.stroke();\n    }\n\n    // Sky gradient\n    const gd = ctx.createLinearGradient(0,0,0,H*0.55);\n    gd.addColorStop(0,\"rgba(0,0,20,0)\"); gd.addColorStop(1,\"rgba(0,0,20,0.55)\");\n    ctx.fillStyle = gd; ctx.fillRect(0,0,W,H*0.55);\n\n    // Sun\n    ctx.save();\n    ctx.translate(W/2, H*0.3);\n    const angle = this.t * 0.4;\n    ctx.rotate(angle);\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#ffbe0b\";\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(0,0,30,0,Math.PI*2); ctx.fill();\n    ctx.restore();\n\n    // Mountains\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#0a0e1c\";\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(0,H*0.5); ctx.quadraticCurveTo(W*0.35,H*0.4,W*0.5,H*0.55); ctx.quadraticCurveTo(W*0.65,H*0.6,W,H*0.5); ctx.closePath(); ctx.fill();\n\n    // Fence posts\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#1a2430\";\n    for (let p = -1; p <= 1; p+=2) {\n      ctx.fillRect(p*2+p*8, H*0.62-12, 4, 20);\n    }\n\n    // Fence rails\n    ctx.strokeStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.18)\"; ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n    for (let p = -1; p <= 1; p+=2) {\n      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(p*2+p*10, H*0.62); ctx.lineTo(p*2+p*10, H*0.7); ctx.stroke();\n    }\n\n    // Road dust\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.04)\";\n    for (let d = -1; d <= 1; d+=2) {\n      ctx.fillRect(d*2+d*12, H*0.62, 2, 6);\n    }\n\n    // Road edge\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"rgba(0,0,0,0.18)\";\n    ctx.fillRect(-2, H*0.58, 2, H*0.32);\n    ctx.fillRect(W, H*0.58, 2, H*0.32);\n\n    // Road edge glow\n    ctx.globalAlpha = 0.18;\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#ffbe0b\";\n    ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \"lighter\";\n    for (let g = -1; g <= 1; g+=2) {\n      ctx.fillRect(g*2+g*12, H*0.62-8, 2, 16);\n    }\n    ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \"source-over\";\n    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;\n\n    // Name\n    title(ctx, \"ROAD RACE\", W/2, H*0.32, { size: 56 });\n\n    // Menu\n    this._drawMenu(ctx);\n\n    // Fade out\n    if (this.alpha < 1) {\n      const gd = ctx.createLinearGradient(0,0,0,H);\n      gd.addColorStop(0,\"rgba(0,0,0,0)\"); gd.addColorStop(1,`rgba(0,0,0,${1-Math.max(0,this.alpha))}`);\n      ctx.fillStyle = gd; ctx.fillRect(0,0,W,H);\n    }\n  }\n}\n```",
