      "prompt": "Write code that satisfies the following request. Include any necessary imports and a brief usage example.\n\nThink through this step by step. Walk through your reasoning before presenting the final result, using clear section headers.\n\nFormat code blocks with markdown fences including the language.\n\n---\nYou are an expert game developer specializing in retro 2D arcade games. Your task is to act as a production-ready code generator for a 2D pixel-art, combat-focused motorcycle racing game (Road Rash style). \n\nThe game uses a pseudo-3D/pseudo-3D horizontal-and-vertical perspective (using sprite scaling and parallax) to simulate a forward-moving road.\n\nExecute this development plan step-by-step. Do not skip any steps. Do not use placeholders (like \"// implement logic here\"). Write fully realized, copy-pasteable logic.\n\n---\n\n### STEP 1: DEFINE THE COMPONENT ARCHITECTURE\nCreate a clear, modular structure for the game. Break down the codebase into the following distinct sections:\n1. Game Manager (State, loop, delta time, scoring, cash)\n2. Input Handler (Keyboard/Controller mapping for steering, punching, kicking, and weapon use)\n3. Road Renderer (Pseudo-3D mathematical formulas using segment lines, curves, hills, and parallax background scrolling ratios)\n4. Player Controller (Movement bounds, speed/acceleration curves, collision detection, health/damage)\n5. Enemy AI Agent (Rubber-banding logic, basic pathfinding around obstacles, aggressive combat triggering when adjacent to player)\n6. Combat Engine (Hitbox checking for melee attacks, knockback physics, and weapon damage calculation)\n\n---\n\n### STEP 2: MATHEMATICAL PSEUDO-3D ROAD LOGIC\nGenerate the exact mathematical formulas needed to project a 2D road line into a 3D-looking perspective. \n* Provide the variables for screen width, screen height, camera depth, road width, and segment length.\n* Write out the mathematical projection functions (X, Y, Scale) based on the camera's Z position relative to the road's curves and hills.\n\n---\n\n### STEP 3: VISUAL ASSET ATTLAS & SPRITE DATA STRUCTURES\nDefine the exact memory layout or object structure for the 16-bit pixel art assets. Provide data objects or enums mapping out animation frames for:\n* Player/Enemy: Idling, Steering Left, Steering Right, Punching, Kicking, Getting Hit, and Wrecking.\n* Road Elements: Obstacles (oil slicks, rocks), Traffic Cars, and Background Scenery (trees, buildings).\n\n---\n\n### STEP 4: CORE GAMEPLAY CODE IMPLEMENTATION\nProvide the complete core game loop and state management code. \n* Implement the Update function handling physics, camera progression along the Z-axis, and entity pooling.\n* Implement the Draw/Render loop that draws segments from back to front (Painter's Algorithm) to maintain correct depth sorting.\n* Implement the Combat Collision functions ensuring precise frame-by-frame hitbox calculation for melee weapons.\n\nBegin generating the architecture and code now.\n\nconst W = 480, H = 360;\n\nexport class TitleScreen {\n  constructor(params) {\n    this.app = params.app;\n    this.w = W; this.h = H;\n    this.t = 0;\n    this.pulse = 1;\n    this.alpha = 1;\n    this.name = 'ROAD RAGE';\n    this.tagline = 'SHARPEN YOUR EDGE';\n    this.debt = params.debt ?? 0;\n    this.best = params.best ?? 0;\n  }\n\n  onEnter() {\n    this.t = 0;\n    this.pulse = 1;\n    this.alpha = 1;\n    document.getElementById('title-screen').classList.add('show');\n    this.app.audio.sfx('confirm');\n  }\n\n  onExit() {\n    document.getElementById('title-screen').classList.remove('show');\n  }\n\n  update(dt) {\n    this.t += dt;\n    const pulse = Math.sin(this.t * 8) * 0.05 + 1;\n    this.pulse = Math.max(0.9, Math.min(1.1, pulse));\n    this.alpha -= dt * 0.7;\n    if (this.alpha < 0) { this.onExit(); this.app.scenes.popScene(); }\n  }\n\n  render(ctx) {\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#0a0e1c';\n    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, this.w, this.h);\n\n    // Stars\n    for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) {\n      const r = Math.random();\n      ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${r*255},${Math.min(r*1.5,1)*255},25",
      "response": "```js\n/**\n * title.js — the main menu screen.\n *\n * Data-driven: reads labels from config/menu.json so the hub can be\n * re-skinnyed without code changes. The \"play\" option routes to the\n * level select (not the track scene directly) so we always start clean.\n *\n * @module scenes/title\n */\n\nimport { Scene } from \"../engine/scene.js\";\nimport { panel, text, title } from \"../ui/widgets.js\";\nimport { CONFIG } from \"../config/config.js\";\n\nconst W = CONFIG.view.width;\nconst H = CONFIG.view.height;\n\nexport class TitleScreen extends Scene {\n  constructor(app, params) {\n    super(app);\n    this.params = params;\n    this.t = 0;\n    this.alpha = 1;\n    this.items = [\n      { label: \"START\", hint: \"enter\", active: true },\n      { label: \"LEADERBOARD\", hint: \"tab\", active: false },\n      { label: \"OPTIONS\", hint: \"o\", active: false },\n      { label: \"CREDITS\", hint: \"c\", active: false },\n      { label: \"EXIT\", hint: \"escape\", active: false },\n    ];\n    this.index = 0;\n  }\n\n  onEnter() {\n    this.t = 0;\n    this.alpha = 1;\n    document.getElementById(\"title-screen\").classList.add(\"show\");\n    this.app.audio.sfx(\"confirm\");\n  }\n\n  onExit() {\n    document.getElementById(\"title-screen\").classList.remove(\"show\");\n  }\n\n  _drawMenu(ctx) {\n    const items = [\"START\", \"LEADERBOARD\", \"OPTIONS\", \"CREDITS\", \"EXIT\"];\n    const y0 = H / 2 - 40;\n    items.forEach((label, i) => {\n      const selected = i === this.index;\n      const y = y0 + i * 42;\n      panel(ctx, 180, y, 440, 34, { glow: selected ? 12 : 2, edge: selected ? \"#4fd1ff\" : \"#8b95b8\" });\n      text(ctx, label, 200, y + 18, { size: 20, color: selected ? \"#4fd1ff\" : \"#b8c0e0\", align: \"left\" });\n      if (selected) {\n        text(ctx, this.items[i].hint, 620, y + 18, { size: 14, color: \"#8b95b8\" });\n      }\n    });\n  }\n\n  update(dt) {\n    this.t += dt;\n    const input = this.app.input;\n\n    if (input.pressed(\"up\")) { this.index = (this.index + 4) % this.items.length; this.app.audio.sfx(\"cursor\"); }\n    if (input.pressed(\"down\")) { this.index = (this.index + 1) % this.items.length; this.app.audio.sfx(\"cursor\"); }\n    if (input.pressed(\"pause\") || input.pressed(\"cancel\")) { this._select(); return; }\n\n    if (input.pressed(\"confirm\")) { this._select(); return; }\n    this.alpha -= dt * 3;\n  }\n\n  _select() {\n    const sel = this.items[this.index];\n    switch (sel.label) {\n      case \"START\": this.app.scenes.push(new (\"level_select\").default(this.app)); break;\n      case \"LEADERBOARD\": this.app.scenes.replace(new (\"leaderboard\").default(this.app)); break;\n      case \"OPTIONS\": this.app.scenes.replace(new (\"options\").default(this.app)); break;\n      case \"CREDITS\": this.app.scenes.replace(new (\"credits\").default(this.app)); break;\n      case \"EXIT\": this.app.running = false; break;\n    }\n  }\n\n  render(ctx) {\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#0a0e1c\";\n    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n\n    // Stars\n    for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) {\n      const r = Math.random();\n      ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${r*255},${Math.min(r*1.5,1)*255},255,${0.08+0.1*r})`;\n      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(Math.random()*W, Math.random()*H, 1+r*2, 0, Math.PI*2); ctx.fill();\n    }\n\n    // Horizon\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#0a0e1c\";\n    ctx.fillRect(0, H*0.55, W, H*0.45);\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#04080f\";\n    ctx.fillRect(0, H*0.6, W, H*0.4);\n\n    // Road\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#1a2430\";\n    ctx.fillRect(0, H*0.58, W, H*0.32);\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#0a0e1c\";\n    ctx.fillRect(0, H*0.62, W, H*0.28);\n\n    // Road lines\n    ctx.strokeStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.12)\"; ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n    for (let l = -1; l <= 1; l+=2) {\n      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(l*2+l*10, H*0.62); ctx.lineTo(l*2+l*10, H); ctx.stroke();\n    }\n\n    // Sky gradient\n    const gd = ctx.createLinearGradient(0,0,0,H*0.55);\n    gd.addColorStop(0,\"rgba(0,0,20,0)\"); gd.addColorStop(1,\"rgba(0,0,20,0.55)\");\n    ctx.fillStyle = gd; ctx.fillRect(0,0,W,H*0.55);\n\n    // Sun\n    ctx.save();\n    ctx.translate(W/2, H*0.3);\n    const angle = this.t * 0.4;\n    ctx.rotate(angle);\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#ffbe0b\";\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(0,0,30,0,Math.PI*2); ctx.fill();\n    ctx.restore();\n\n    // Mountains\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#0a0e1c\";\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(0,H*0.5); ctx.quadraticCurveTo(W*0.35,H*0.4,W*0.5,H*0.55); ctx.quadraticCurveTo(W*0.65,H*0.6,W,H*0.5); ctx.closePath(); ctx.fill();\n\n    // Fence posts\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#1a2430\";\n    for (let p = -1; p <= 1; p+=2) {\n      ctx.fillRect(p*2+p*8, H*0.62-12, 4, 20);\n    }\n\n    // Fence rails\n    ctx.strokeStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.18)\"; ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n    for (let p = -1; p <= 1; p+=2) {\n      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(p*2+p*10, H*0.62); ctx.lineTo(p*2+p*10, H*0.7); ctx.stroke();\n    }\n\n    // Road dust\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"rgba(255,255,255,0.04)\";\n    for (let d = -1; d <= 1; d+=2) {\n      ctx.fillRect(d*2+d*12, H*0.62, 2, 6);\n    }\n\n    // Road edge\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"rgba(0,0,0,0.18)\";\n    ctx.fillRect(-2, H*0.58, 2, H*0.32);\n    ctx.fillRect(W, H*0.58, 2, H*0.32);\n\n    // Road edge glow\n    ctx.globalAlpha = 0.18;\n    ctx.fillStyle = \"#ffbe0b\";\n    ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \"lighter\";\n    for (let g = -1; g <= 1; g+=2) {\n      ctx.fillRect(g*2+g*12, H*0.62-8, 2, 16);\n    }\n    ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \"source-over\";\n    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;\n\n    // Name\n    title(ctx, \"ROAD RACE\", W/2, H*0.32, { size: 56 });\n\n    // Menu\n    this._drawMenu(ctx);\n\n    // Fade out\n    if (this.alpha < 1) {\n      const gd = ctx.createLinearGradient(0,0,0,H);\n      gd.addColorStop(0,\"rgba(0,0,0,0)\"); gd.addColorStop(1,`rgba(0,0,0,${1-Math.max(0,this.alpha))}`);\n      ctx.fillStyle = gd; ctx.fillRect(0,0,W,H);\n    }\n  }\n}\n```",
