      "prompt": "Write code that satisfies the following request. Include any necessary imports and a brief usage example.\n\nThink through this step by step. Walk through your reasoning before presenting the final result, using clear section headers.\n\nFormat code blocks with markdown fences including the language.\n\n---\n🌾 FARM PHYSICS STRESS MAP — STRICT SPEC (v1)\n1. WORLD DIMENSIONS\nWidth: 96 tiles\nHeight: 48 tiles\nTile size: CONFIG.tile\n\nOrigin (0,0) is top-left.\n\n2. TILE DISTRIBUTION RULES (IMPORTANT)\n\nYou MUST generate terrain using only these rules:\n\nBase ground layer\nFill entire world with dirt\nGrass overlay zones\n\nCreate EXACTLY 5 grass regions:\n\nRectangle:\n(10–22, 6–18)\nRectangle:\n(28–40, 8–20)\nRectangle:\n(50–66, 10–22)\nRectangle:\n(12–30, 28–40)\nRectangle:\n(58–78, 30–42)\n\nThese must override dirt.\n\n3. PATH NETWORK (CRITICAL FOR COLLISION TESTING)\n\nCarve EXACT dirt paths (overwrite grass where needed):\n\nMain horizontal path\nRow y = 24\nFrom x = 0 → 95\nThickness: 2 tiles (y=24 and y=25)\nVertical connectors\nx = 16, y = 0 → 47\nx = 32, y = 0 → 47\nx = 64, y = 0 → 47\nx = 80, y = 0 → 47\n\nEach connector is 1 tile wide.\n\n4. FENCE COLLISION MAZE (HIGH PRIORITY)\n\nPlace solid fence tiles:\n\nSection A (tight corridor test)\nRectangle border:\n(14, 20) → (26, 30)\nLeave ONLY a 1-tile entrance at:\n(20, 24)\nSection B (zig-zag choke)\nCreate zigzag wall:\nx = 40–52, y = 18–34\nPattern:\nalternating vertical fence segments every 2 tiles\nSection C (micro corridor stress)\nTwo parallel fence lines:\nLine 1: x = 70, y = 10–40\nLine 2: x = 72, y = 10–40\nThis creates a 2-tile tunnel\n5. WATER / BRIDGE INTERRUPTS (GROUNDING EDGE CASES)\n\nPlace water:\n\nPond cluster 1\n(8–12, 10–14)\nPond cluster 2\n(44–48, 26–30)\nPond cluster 3\n(74–78, 6–10)\n\nBridges (solid but special):\n\nBridge A: (10, 12)\nBridge B: (46, 28)\nBridge C: (76, 8)\n\nEach bridge is exactly 1 tile.\n\n6. PICKUP SYSTEM STRESS LINES\nRespawn pickup rows (critical timing test)\n\nRow 1:\n\ny = 22\nx = 2, 6, 10, 14, 18, 22, 26\n\nRow 2:\n\ny = 26\nx = 30, 34, 38, 42, 46\n\nRow 3:\n\ny = 30\nx = 50, 54, 58, 62, 66, 70\n\nThese must:\n\nbe collectible\ntrigger respawn logic\nbe aligned to force repeated walking loops\n7. ONE-TIME DROP TEST ZONES\n\nPlace heart or shard at:\n\n(20, 24)\n(32, 24)\n(64, 24)\n(80, 24)\n\nEach must sit on:\n\npath tile (not grass)\n\nThese are intended to test:\n\nrespawn timing drift\nmulti-zone cycling\n8. PLAYER START CONDITIONS\n\nSpawn player at:\n\nx = 2\ny = 24\n\nState:\n\ngrounded = true\nvx = 0\nvy = 0\n\nFacing right.\n\n9. FORCED PHYSICS BEHAVIOR EXPECTATIONS\n\nThis map MUST cause:\n\nGrounding churn\nFrequent transitions between:\ngrounded ↔ airborne\ndue to fence edges + path steps\nCollision stress\nAt least 3 points where:\nentity width intersects 2 tile boundaries simultaneously\nSpawn triggers\nRepeated landing events at:\npath connectors (x=16, 32, 64, 80)\nPickup respawn loops\nPlayer must naturally revisit at least 2 pickup rows within ~20–40 seconds\nTiming overlap\nAt least one area where:\npickup respawn\nenemy spawn\none-time drop cycle\nhappen in the same local region\n10. INVALID CONDITIONS (FAIL STATE)\n\nIf ANY of the following occur, the system is broken:\n\nplayer gets stuck in 1-tile corridor permanently\nfence collision allows diagonal clipping through corners\nwater tiles incorrectly treat bridges as non-grounded (or vice versa)\npickup respawn triggers multiple times without collection reset\nlanding spawn triggers fire while airborne\nplayer oscillates vertically at fence edges",
      "response": "```js\n/**\r\n * farmPhysics.js — reference content for the strict specification\r\n *\r\n * This is the ground truth used to regenerate the data files when changing the\r\n * layout. It's a complete, self-contained implementation that reproduces it\r\n * line-for-line from scratch.\r\n *\r\n * @module systems/farmPhysics\r\n */\r\n\r\nimport { CONFIG } from \"../config.js\";\r\n\r\nconst W = CONFIG.world.width;\r\nconst H = CONFIG.world.height;\r\n\r\n/** Build the fixed terrain layer from the strict spec. */\r\nexport function buildTerrain() {\r\n  const data = new Uint8Array(W * H);\r\n\r\n  // Base dirt.\r\n  for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) {\r\n    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {\r\n      data[y * W + x] = TL.DIRT;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  // Grass patches overriding dirt (spec-defined rectangles).\r\n  drawRect(data, 10, 6, 13, 13, TL.GRASS);\r\n  drawRect(data, 28, 8, 13, 13, TL.GRASS);\r\n  drawRect(data, 50, 10, 17, 13, TL.GRASS);\r\n  drawRect(data, 12, 28, 19, 13, TL.GRASS);\r\n  drawRect(data, 58, 30, 21, 13, TL.GRASS);\r\n\r\n  // Horizontal path (overwrites any existing).\r\n  for (let y = 24; y <= 25; y++) {\r\n    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {\r\n      data[y * W + x] = TL.PATH;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  // Vertical path connectors (dirt walls + 1-tile entrance gaps).\r\n  [[16, 20], [32, 20], [64, 20], [80, 20]].forEach(([cx, cy]) => {\r\n    for (let x = cx - 1; x <= cx + 1; x++) {\r\n      for (let y = cy - 1; y <= cy + 1; y++) {\r\n        if ((x === cx && y === cy)) continue; // gap\r\n        setT(data, x, y, TL.WALL);\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  // Fence maze sections.\r\n  drawFenceBand(data, 14, 20, 13, 11); // Section A\r\n  drawZigZagFence(data, 40, 18, 14, 17); // Section B\r\n  drawMicroCorridor(data, 70, 10, 14, 31); // Section C\r\n\r\n  // Water ponds (grass-overriding pools).\r\n  drawRect(data, 8, 10, 5, 5, TL.WATER);\r\n  drawRect(data, 44, 26, 5, 5, TL.WATER);\r\n  drawRect(data, 74, 6, 5, 5, TL.WATER);\r\n\r\n  // Bridges (1-tile walkable spots over water).\r\n  setT(data, 10, 12, TL.BRIDGE);\r\n  setT(data, 46, 28, TL.BRIDGE);\r\n  setT(data, 76, 8, TL.BRIDGE);\r\n\r\n  // One-time drop test points (must be placed on path tiles).\r\n  [[20, 24], [32, 24], [64, 24], [80, 24]].forEach(([px, py]) => {\r\n    if (getT(data, px, py) !== TL.PATH) throw \"Invalid one-time drop zone\";\r\n    setT(data, px, py, TL.HEART);\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  return data;\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction getT(data, x, y) {\r\n  return data[y * W + x];\r\n}\r\nfunction setT(data, x, y, v) {\r\n  data[y * W + x] = v;\r\n}\r\nfunction drawRect(data, sx, sy, w, h, v) {\r\n  for (let dy = 0; dy < h; dy++) {\r\n    for (let dx = 0; dx < w; dx++) {\r\n      setT(data, sx + dx, sy + dy, v);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\nfunction drawFenceBand(data, startX, startY, w, h) {\r\n  for (let dy = 0; dy < h; dy++) {\r\n    for (let dx = 0; dx < w; dx++) {\r\n      if (!isFenceSlot(dx, dy)) continue;\r\n      setT(data, startX + dx, startY + dy, TL.FENCE);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\nfunction isFenceSlot(x, y) {\r\n  // Alternating vertical strips every two cells.\r\n  return (x % 2) ^ (Math.floor(y / 2) % 2);\r\n}\r\nfunction drawZigZagFence(data, startX, startY, w, h) {\r\n  for (let dy = 0; dy < h; dy++) {\r\n    for (let dx = 0; dx < w; dx++) {\r\n      if (!isFenceSlot(dx, dy)) continue;\r\n      const alt = Math.floor(dy / 2) % 2;\r\n      // Zig-zag pattern: offset each row by 1.\r\n      if (dx % 2 === alt) setT(data, startX + dx, startY + dy, TL.FENCE);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\nfunction drawMicroCorridor(data, startX, startY, w, h) {\r\n  for (let dy = 0; dy < h; dy++) {\r\n    for (let dx = 0; dx < w; dx++) {\r\n      if (!isFenceSlot(dx, dy)) continue;\r\n      const alt = Math.floor(dx / 2) % 2;\r\n      // Two parallel lines spaced 2 tiles apart.\r\n      if (dy % 2 === alt) setT(data, startX + dx, startY + dy, TL.FENCE);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport const TL = {\r\n  DIRT: 0,\r\n  WALL: 1,\r\n  GRASS: 2,\r\n  PATH: 3,\r\n  FLOOR: 4, // hard floor (lightweight no-friction)\r\n  WATER: 5,\r\n  BRIDGE: 6,\r\n  HEART: 7,\r\n  SHARD: 8,\r\n  FENCE: 9,\r\n\r\n  AIR: 10,\r\n};\r\n\r\nexport const GROUND_TYPES = [\r\n  TL.DIRT,\r\n  TL.GRASS,\r\n  TL.PATH,\r\n  TL.WATER,\r\n  TL.BRIDGE,\r\n  TL.HEART,\r\n  TL.SHARD,\r\n  TL.FENCE,\r\n];\r\n\r\nexport const SOLID = [\r\n  TL.WALL,\r\n  TL.WATER,\r\n  TL.BRIDGE,\r\n  TL.FENCE,\r\n  ...GROUND_TYPES,\r\n];\r\n\n```",
