      "id": "8f6e5206-74c9-4949-91a0-e2e15da2d39e",
      "tab": "code",
      "task": "explain",
      "provider": "ollama",
      "model": "mycoder-v0.2",
      "prompt": "Explain what the following code does. Cover its overall purpose, then walk through the important parts.\n\nThink through this step by step. Walk through your reasoning before presenting the final result, using clear section headers.\n\nFormat code blocks with markdown fences including the language.\n\n---\n“Simulate 50 years in this world without player input. What systems run and how do they interact?”",
      "response": "```js\n// ── Simulates 50 real seconds worth of the world on the main thread for the demo.\n//    Every system updates every frame: audio, physics, particles, camera, AI,\n//    enemies, pickups, dialogue, stats. No player movement or interaction is\n//    simulated so it feels \"passive\" while keeping the engine running.\nexport function simulateDemoFrame() {\n  const dt = Math.min(1 / 20, performance.now() / 1000 - lastFrameTime) * 0.9;\n  lastFrameTime = performance.now() / 1000;\n\n  updateAudio(dt);\n  Physics.update(dt);\n  particleUpdate(dt);\n  Camera.update();\n\n  // Dialogue runs every frame to advance timed lines that don't require input.\n  if (Dialogue.running) Dialogue.update(dt);\n\n  // Stats track continuous values every second — no need to poll each one per\n  // frame but reading them is cheap and gives the same result. Only health\n  // needs special handling as it drains naturally over time.\n  const now = performance.now();\n  if (lastStatsTs + 1000 <= now) {\n    lastStatsTs = now;\n    const s = G.stats;\n    s.maxHp     = G.maxHp;\n    s.hp        = G.hp;\n    s.shards    = G.shards;\n    s.emblems   = G.emblems;\n    s.depth     = G.floor;\n    s.seedsGathered = G.seedsGathered;\n    s.plantings = G.plantingsDone;\n    s.composts  = G.compostPlaced;\n    s.watered   = G.tilesWatered;\n    s.deaths    = G.enemiesKilled;\n    s.products  = G.productsHarvested;\n    s.carrots   = G.carrotsPicked;\n    s.gathered  = G.gatheredHerbs;\n    s.stone     = G.stonesFound;\n    s.echoes    = G.echoesCollected;\n    s.derivedEmblemProgression(); // update derived % completion\n    s.deriveRank(); // recompute the rank based on latest stats\n    // Natural HP drain every second.\n    if (s.hp > 0 && G.hp > 0) G.hp -= G.config.hpDrain * dt;\n    if (G.hp < 0) G.hp = 0;\n  }\n\n  // Enemies naturally respawn after their lifetime.\n  _naturalEnemySpawn(dt);\n\n  // Timed pickups respawn after 3-6 seconds (same as collectible respawn).\n  _timedPickupRespawn(dt);\n\n  // One-time \"emblem drop\" events (hearthstone, echo shard, guide log)\n  _spawnOneTimeDrops(dt);\n\n  // The emerald vine spreads continuously, drawing the ground tile by tile.\n  Vines.update(dt);\n\n  // Persistent fog fades towards the end.\n  Fog.update();\n\n  // Wind phase shifts every 20s for the swinging lights.\n  const t = (performance.now() / 1000) % 40;\n  G.windPhase = ((t / 40) + 0.75) % 1;\n\n  // Audio snapshots update every second so music keeps stepping with the world.\n  Music.audioSnapshot(G);\n\n  // AI hearts pulse slowly so they're still visible when not actively attacking.\n  _aiHeartbeat(dt);\n}\n```",
