      "prompt": "Explain what the following code does. Cover its overall purpose, then walk through the important parts.\n\nBe direct and concise. Lead with the result/code and keep explanation to a minimum.\n\nFormat code blocks with markdown fences including the language.\n\n---\ngo into deep deep detail",
      "response": "```go\n// stream_writer.go — buffered write+flush: efficient, non-blocking I/O\n\ntype StreamWriter struct {\n  buf []byte   // internal buffer\n  pos int      // read/write position in buf\n  done bool     // flush() already wrote full contents\n  closed bool   // Close() was called (write panics on closed streams)\n  dst WriteAt  // underlying storage (file, pipe, memory, ...)\n  err error    // permanent failure; all writes silently discard after this\n}\n\nfunc NewStreamWriter(dst WriteAt) *StreamWriter {\n  return &StreamWriter{buf:make([]byte,4096),dst:dst}\n}\n\n// Append data to our buffer. Returns bytes accepted (<= len(data)), never fails.\nfunc (w *StreamWriter) append(data []byte) int {\n  if w.done || w.closed { return 0 }\n  want := len(w.buf) - w.pos\n  n := copy(w.buf[w.pos:], data)\n  if n > want { n = want }\n  w.pos += n\n  return n\n}\n\n// Flush whatever is in the buffer to the underlying storage.\n// Always returns the total number of bytes written since creation.\nfunc (w *StreamWriter) Flush() (total uint64, _ error) {\n  if w.done || w.closed { return }\n  start := uint64(w.dst.bytesWritten())\n  for {\n    n, e := w.dst.Write(w.buf[:w.pos])\n    if n > 0 { w.pos -= n }\n    total += uint64(n)\n    if n > 0 && e == nil { continue } // partial writes: try again\n    if n == 0 && e == nil { break }    // EOF (shouldn't happen here)\n    w.err = e; w.done = true; break\n  }\n  return\n}\n\n// Permanent close marker; writes past this point panic. Idempotent.\nfunc (w *StreamWriter) Close() {\n  if !w.closed {\n    w.Flush()\n    w.closed = true\n  }\n}\n```",
