      "prompt": "You are helping with the following request:\n\ni am wanting to build a racing game that includes boost, a banana that when you drive over it, it inverts the controls, and i want it to have a 3 lap track that goes in the shape of a heart. give me the breakdown of how to build this game.\n\n\nRespond using exactly these markdown section headers, in this order, each followed by concise content (use bullet points where helpful):\n\n## Overview\n## Key Components\n## Dependencies\n## Open Questions\n\nDo not add any extra top-level headers or preamble text before the first header.",
      "response": "## Overview\nBuild a racing game with a boost mechanic, an inverted-controls banana bonus, and a heart-shaped 3-lap track.\n\n## Key Components\n- Player car physics\n- Track generation (heart shape)\n- Boost system\n- Banana bonus\n- Inverted controls\n- Lap counter\n- Timer\n- Scoring\n- User interface\n- Game loop\n- Collision detection\n- Audio feedback\n- Responsive design for mobile/tablet/desktop\n\n## Dependencies\n- Phaser 3 library\n- WebAudio API for audio\n- Modern browser (ES6+ features)\n\n## Open Questions\n- How should the boost work? A short burst or a sustained speed increase?\n- What is the best way to implement the banana's inversion effect?\n- Should there be visual indicators for boosts and bananas?",
