      "model": "mycoder-tuned-14b",
      "prompt": "You are helping with the following request:\n\nbuild me a design for agent to build a simple farming loop\n\n\nRespond using exactly these markdown section headers, in this order, each followed by concise content (use bullet points where helpful):\n\n## Overview\n## Key Components\n## Dependencies\n## Open Questions\n\nDo not add any extra top-level headers or preamble text before the first header.",
      "response": "## Overview\nThe goal is to create a simple farming loop that generates crops based on season and player inventory, tracks growth over time, and yields products when ready.\n\n## Key Components\n- `getSeason`: Determines current season based on game day.\n- `cropSchedule`: Season-specific crop planting schedule.\n- `cropGrowthRate`: Days required for crops to grow from seed to harvest.\n- `farmTileIds`: Valid tile IDs for planting.\n- `canPlantSeed`: Checks if a seed can be planted at a given position.\n- `plantSeed`: Plants a seed at the specified position, updating state and cooldown.\n- `updateCropGrowth`: Advances crop growth daily.\n- `harvestCrop`: Harvests ripe crops, removing seeds and adding products to inventory.\n- `_growProduct`: Generates product drops from harvested crops.\n\n## Dependencies\n- `getSeason`\n- `cropSchedule`, `cropGrowthRate`\n- `FARM_TILE_IDS`, `SEED_ITEM_ID`, `PRODUCT_ITEM_ID`\n\n## Open Questions\n- Should the growing logic support partial progress tracking (e.g., watered but not fully grown)?\n- How should multiple adjacent plots of the same crop behave?\n- What feedback should players receive during the growing period?",
