      "prompt": "You are helping with the following request:\n\nim wanting to build an arcade racer but i need a prompt directed specifically at you to understand the request of\n\n\nRespond using exactly these markdown section headers, in this order, each followed by concise content (use bullet points where helpful):\n\n## Overview\n## Key Components\n## Dependencies\n## Open Questions\n\nDo not add any extra top-level headers or preamble text before the first header.",
      "response": "## Overview\nDevelop an arcade-style racing game using modern web technologies like HTML5 Canvas and JavaScript.\n\n## Key Components\n- Player car: controlled by WASD or arrow keys\n- Enemies: multiple types moving towards the player\n- Track: static layout with configurable curves and straightaways\n- Camera: fixed overhead view\n- Scrolling background: realistic track details\n- Collision detection: cars stop when they touch\n- Score: distance traveled over time\n- Lives system: lose a life if hit by enemy\n- Power-ups: randomly appear on track\n- Timer: countdown adds pressure\n- Start screen\n- Game over screen\n- HUD: score, lives, timer displayed above track\n\n## Dependencies\n- Webpack for module bundling\n- Emscripten compiler for running C/C++ code\n- Three.js for 3D track rendering\n- PixiJS for canvas-based UI elements\n\n## Open Questions\n- Should enemies use physics or pure collision detection?\n- How many lanes should there be? Two or three?\n- What types of power-ups should exist?\n- Should there be obstacles in addition to enemies?",
