lator that performs basic mathematical calculations (addition) based on user input. It continues to prompt the user until explicitly instructed to exit by typing \"exit\". The code could be extended with more operations and error handling for non-numeric inputs or division by zero errors, among other improvements.\n\n# Improvements: \nHere are some possible enhancements that can make this calculator better:\n1. Input validation - Ensure the user enters valid numeric values before performing calculations to avoid runtime errors.\n2. Extend operations – Add more arithmetic functions like multiplication and division, as well as other mathematical functions if desired (e.g., power or square root). \n3. Error handling - Implement try-except blocks for error management in case of invalid inputs such as strings when expecting numbers.\n4. User experience enhancements – Provide a clear menu with options and instructions, possibly using loops to continuously offer choices until the user decides to exit or perform calculations multiple times without restarting the program. \n5. Persistence - Save results for repeated use within same session (or even across sessions) by storing them in variables that persist beyond individual operations.",
